# Runner / configs conventions

## CLI parallelism

`run` / `run-all` accept `--jobs N` (`benchmark.scb_run.run_matrix`). Default `1` is serial; for real experiments use `--jobs` up to `arms × runs` (see core rule). Check all locally available Docker images first and reuse any compatible image; pull or build only if no suitable local image exists (see core rule).

New skill arms must pass **CP1 smoke** before full runs:

```bash
uv run python -m benchmark smoke --arm <name>
```

`run` / `run-all` call `require_smoke_validated` and exit unless `harnesses/<arm>/SMOKE.json` is ok (or `--skip-smoke-check`).

## Invoking SCB

Entry: `python -m benchmark.scb_main` (not raw `slop-code` alone) so hooks/env apply.  
Env always set for runs:

- `SCBENCH_PROBLEMS_PATH` → `vendor/scb-problems`
- `SCBENCH_HOME` → per-run `.scbench_home`
- `DOCKER_CONFIG` → per-run empty auth config
- `HB_ENABLE_PONYTAIL=1` only for ponytail arm
- `PYTHONPATH` includes `harness_sitecustomize` + repo root

Agent config: `configs/agent_codex.yaml` (default) or `configs/agent_opencode.yaml`.
Versions must match Docker-installed CLI pins in `vendor/pins.json`.

## Model / provider flags

```text
# Codex default (unchanged)
--agent codex   # optional; this is the default
# → SCB --model codex_auth/<model>

# OpenCode (provider + model required)
--agent opencode --provider opencode_auth --model deepseek-v4-flash-free
# → SCB --model opencode_auth/deepseek-v4-flash-free
```

Not `openai/...` unless `OPENAI_API_KEY` is intentionally used.

## Ponytail injection

`benchmark/ponytail_hook.py` copies pinned `harnesses/ponytail/SKILL.md` into Codex mount `~/.codex/skills/ponytail/` and writes `harness_activation.json` into artifacts. Keep activation mechanism recorded in that JSON.

## Configs

Arm YAMLs use `save_dir` / `save_template`, `pass_policy: all-core-cases`.  
Prompt for ponytail must keep the activation phrase expected by `benchmark.paths.ACTIVATION_PHRASE`.

## Metrics nulls

If a token/cost field is missing from the adapter → store `null`. Never invent approximations for usage.
